      ],
      "summary": "`@tangleai/os/authoring` is the model-free half of the assistant writing an application: `authoringCrib()` (the grammar rules, Jaren's own operator names, each compiled by a test, and a working to-do list), `gateAuthoredApp` (lint, compile, first frame: what to send back for repair), `checkAuthoredApp` with probes that use an application as a person would (a field or button found by its label, placeholder or text), and `authoredManifest`, a document module that asks for nothing. A new instrument, `benchmark/authoring.ts`, measures how often a plain request becomes an application that works when a person uses it: 22 of 24 with Claude Haiku 5.5 (docs/AUTHORING_BENCHMARK.md).",
      "id": "authoring"
    }
  ],
